  "note": "PATHS ARE THE RUN'S OWN OUT-DIR, spelled abstractly: the frames a run writes land in the directory its invocation names, and no machine's absolute path is committed. FOUR DELTAS AGAINST `live-run-before.json`, all of them the remediation rounds': the slot is still released (`slotPresent: false`); conversation B - a live-but-EMPTY queue - is offered its door (`headerTrigger: 1`, was 0), the capability read aligned to the wire contract (R3/Q1); `onDraft` (step 7) shows that a session-scoped drawer does not follow onto a route with no conversation (UX U1); and `onEmptyPane`/`afterEmptyPaneEscape` (step 8) are the zero-row pane's own readings - the keyboard lands ON the surface (`activeTag: SECTION`, `activeLabel: \"This conversation's asks\"`, `activeIsTheDoor: false`) and an Escape from there closes it (`drawers: 0`). Before round 2's landing fix every one of those four readings was the opposite. The live frames are re-taken at this head; their visible content differs from the round-1 pass only in the live clock text they carry (relative times, a countdown)."
